I've written the plan for Day 246 (11:03) as two task files in session_plan/. The commit step failed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so git add refused it. The files are on disk for the next phases to read, but nothing was committed.

Task 1: Part of #1111. yoyo commit and /commit will refuse a flag they don't know instead of putting it in the commit message. The assessment reproduced this: yoyo commit --ammend made a new commit titled --ammend. It's the one member of #1111 that changes git history.
• Unknown flags exit 2 with a "did you mean" hint (--ammend → --amend). The shell and the REPL use the same refusal message.
• -m <words> and --message <words> are accepted the way git accepts them, because refusing them would make every git user retype.
• Anything after -- goes into the message unchanged, so a message that really starts with - can still be written.
• Tests go in a new sibling file, src/commands_git_commit_args_tests.rs. commands_git.rs is exactly at its recorded size in the size gate (tests/module_size.rs).
• One test uses a temporary repo with a staged change and checks that --ammend exits 2 and creates no commit.
• After committing, the task posts a comment on #1111 saying the commit row is fixed and listing what's still open, with init next (it writes YOYO.md).

Task 2: Fixes #1112. This is the backlog-drain slot; #1112 has the least work left of the 19 open issues. The flag scans that run before -- is handled (--no-color, --no-bell, --no-notify and --no-rtk in main.rs, and --quiet/-q and --print in cli.rs) will each switch to the existing option_args, a one-token change per scan. The list comes from a census recorded on #1112.
• Test pairs cover the same flag before -- (still applied) and after it (not applied, and still sent to the prompt as written).
• One check temporarily reverts a scan and confirms its test fails, then restores it.
• The separate case where yoyo -p --help prints the help page gets its own issue before the push, so it still has an open ticket after #1112 closes.

No release: it isn't due (12 days, 51 commits). Both tasks are about refusing mistyped flags, so they're better released together with the rest of #1111.

Issues: there were no community issues today. My replies on #1111 and #1112 are in session_plan/issue_responses.md.
